| Stage                                     | Description                                                            | Transition Trigger                              |
| ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| 1️⃣ **NEW**                               | Thread object is created but not yet started.                          | When you create thread using `new Thread()`     |
| 2️⃣ **RUNNABLE**                          | Thread is ready to run or waiting for CPU.                             | When `start()` is called                        |
| 3️⃣ **RUNNING**                           | Thread is currently executing its `run()` method.                      | When CPU picks it from scheduler                |
| 4️⃣ **BLOCKED / WAITING / TIMED_WAITING** | Thread is temporarily inactive — waiting for resource, sleep, or join. | When `sleep()`, `join()`, or waiting for a lock |
| 5️⃣ **TERMINATED (DEAD)**                 | Thread has finished execution.                                         | When `run()` method completes                   |

       +--------+
       |  NEW   |  ---> created using new Thread()
       +--------+
            |
        start()
            ↓
       +------------+
       |  RUNNABLE  | ---> waiting for CPU time
       +------------+
            |
        CPU schedules
            ↓
       +-----------+
       |  RUNNING  | ---> executing run() method
       +-----------+
         |      |
   sleep()/wait() | run() completes
         ↓      ↓
 +--------------------+     +--------------+
 | WAITING/BLOCKED    |     | TERMINATED   |
 +--------------------+     +--------------+

 NEW:
 Thread t = new Thread(() -> System.out.println("Hello"));
 
 RUNNABLE:
 t.start(); // now RUNNABLE
 
 RUNNING
 When the CPU scheduler picks the thread, it becomes RUNNING.
 Executes the run() method.
 This state is managed by JVM and OS — you cannot force it manually
 
 WAITING / BLOCKED / TIMED_WAITING
 | Method                            | State                   |
| --------------------------------- | ----------------------- |
| `sleep(ms)`                       | TIMED_WAITING           |
| `join()`                          | WAITING / TIMED_WAITING |
| `wait()`                          | WAITING                 |
| Waiting for lock (`synchronized`) | BLOCKED                 |
 
 
TERMINATED (DEAD)
Thread finishes its task and exits the run() method.
Cannot be restarted (calling start() again → IllegalThreadStateException).